      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "For reference, the positional ones are tedious to deprecate, so that can be done later, maybe via `OBJ_NAMED_PARAMS`, if possible, but that will be a larger breaking change than this, so I'll leave it for later.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/test/functional/wallet_balance.py b/test/functional/wallet_balance.py\r\nindex 2d36291..f77f9ed 100755\r\n--- a/test/functional/wallet_balance.py\r\n+++ b/test/functional/wallet_balance.py\r\n@@ -85,3 +85,3 @@ class WalletTest(BitcoinTestFramework):\r\n         assert_equal(self.nodes[0].getbalance(minconf=0), 50)\r\n-        assert_equal(self.nodes[0].getbalance(\"*\", 1, True), 50)\r\n+        assert_equal(self.nodes[0].getbalance(dummy=\"*\", minconf=1, include_watchonly=True), 50)\r\n         assert_equal(self.nodes[1].getbalance(minconf=0), 50)\r\ndiff --git a/test/functional/wallet_listreceivedby.py b/test/functional/wallet_listreceivedby.py\r\nindex 3a6a6df..7251576 100755\r\n--- a/test/functional/wallet_listreceivedby.py\r\n+++ b/test/functional/wallet_listreceivedby.py\r\n@@ -78,3 +78,3 @@ class ReceivedByTest(BitcoinTestFramework):\r\n         # Another address receive money\r\n-        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(0, True, True)\r\n+        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(minconf=0, include_empty=True, include_watchonly=True)\r\n         assert_equal(len(res), 2 + num_cb_reward_addresses)  # Right now 2 entries\r\n@@ -85,3 +85,3 @@ class ReceivedByTest(BitcoinTestFramework):\r\n         expected = {\"address\": addr, \"label\": \"\", \"amount\": Decimal(\"0.1\"), \"confirmations\": 11, \"txids\": [txid, ]}\r\n-        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(0, True, True, addr)\r\n+        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(minconf=0, include_empty=True, include_watchonly=True, address_filter=addr)\r\n         assert_array_result(res, {\"address\": addr}, expected)\r\n@@ -90,3 +90,3 @@ class ReceivedByTest(BitcoinTestFramework):\r\n         expected = {\"address\": other_addr, \"label\": \"\", \"amount\": Decimal(\"0.1\"), \"confirmations\": 1, \"txids\": [txid2, ]}\r\n-        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(0, True, True, other_addr)\r\n+        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(minconf=0, include_empty=True, include_watchonly=True, address_filter=other_addr)\r\n         assert_array_result(res, {\"address\": other_addr}, expected)\r\n@@ -94,3 +94,3 @@ class ReceivedByTest(BitcoinTestFramework):\r\n         # Should be two entries though without filter\r\n-        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(0, True, True)\r\n+        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(minconf=0, include_empty=True, include_watchonly=True)\r\n         assert_equal(len(res), 3 + num_cb_reward_addresses)  # Became 3 entries\r\n@@ -99,3 +99,3 @@ class ReceivedByTest(BitcoinTestFramework):\r\n         other_addr = self.nodes[0].getnewaddress()  # note on node[0]! just a random addr\r\n-        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(0, True, True, other_addr)\r\n+        res = self.nodes[1].listreceivedbyaddress(minconf=0, include_empty=True, include_watchonly=True, address_filter=other_addr)\r\n         assert_equal(len(res), 0)\r\n```\r\n\r\n• ### Flag\r\n\r\n  Use one value, -deprecatedrpc=watchonly, for the six RPCs. With it, accept their legacy positional signatures. Without it, reject those signatures with a deprecation error. The new options forms work either way.\r\n\r\n  ### RPC arguments\r\n\r\n   RPC                      Legacy positional arguments, in order                                                           New form\r\n  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\r\n   getbalance               dummy?, minconf, include_watchonly, avoid_reuse                                                 options={minconf, avoid_reuse}\r\n  ───────────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n   listreceivedbyaddress    minconf, include_empty, include_watchonly, address_filter?, include_immature_coinbase           options={minconf, include_empty, address_filter, include_immature_coinbase}\r\n  ───────────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n   listreceivedbylabel      minconf, include_empty, include_watchonly, include_immature_coinbase                            options={minconf, include_empty, include_immature_coinbase}\r\n  ───────────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n   listtransactions         label?, count, skip, include_watchonly                                                          label?, options={count, skip}\r\n  ───────────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n   listsinceblock           blockhash?, target_confirmations, include_watchonly, include_removed, include_change, label?    blockhash?, options={target_confirmations, include_removed, include_change, label}\r\n  ───────────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n   gettransaction           txid, include_watchonly, verbose                                                                txid, options={verbose}\r\n\r\n  ### Proposed parsing approach\r\n\r\n  Keep OBJ_NAMED_PARAMS for the new options, with skip_type_check on the options argument so the positional parser can also receive the old scalar at that position. Add optional trailing legacy slots so the RPC’s fixed\r\n  argument-count check accepts old calls. In each RPC, distinguish an options object from a legacy scalar; gate the legacy path with rpcEnableDeprecated(\"watchonly\"), validate its old arguments, ignore include_watchonly, and\r\n  use the remaining values in their old positions.\r\n\r\n  Named parameters should still be collected into the options object by OBJ_NAMED_PARAMS. Deprecated named fields such as include_watchonly would need to remain in metadata for conversion and be gated in the handler. The\r\n  hidden legacy slots need care because the current named-argument mapping also sees hidden arguments; this approach is a sketch that would need a focused implementation check.\r\n",
